---
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A reusable ESP32-S3 robot controller PCB for Science Olympiad Robot Tour and Electric Vehicle."
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://rsms.me/" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://rsms.me/inter/inter.css" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Robot Template</title>
  </head>

  <body
    class="bg-[#0b1126] text-slate-200 selection:bg-[#aaccff] selection:text-[#113399]"
  >
    <div
      class="mx-auto min-h-screen max-w-screen-xl px-6 py-12 md:px-12 md:py-16 lg:py-0"
    >
      <div class="lg:flex lg:justify-between lg:gap-16">
        <header
          class="lg:sticky lg:top-0 lg:flex lg:h-screen lg:w-[38%] lg:min-w-[360px] lg:flex-col lg:justify-center lg:py-16 mb-10"
        >
          <div
            class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-8 shadow-2xl shadow-blue-950/20 backdrop-blur"
          >
            <div
              class="absolute -right-20 -top-20 h-56 w-56 rounded-full bg-blue-500/10 blur-3xl"
            >
            </div>

            <p
              class="mb-6 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Project Writeup
            </p>

            <h1
              class="mb-4 text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl"
            >
              Robot<br />Template
            </h1>

            <p class="max-w-sm text-base leading-7 text-slate-400">
              A reusable PCB for Science Olympiad robots, designed to make
              future builds more reliable and repeatable.
            </p>

            <nav class="mt-8 hidden lg:block">
              <div class="space-y-5">
                <a
                  href="#overview"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Overview
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#requirements"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Requirements
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#electronics"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Electronics
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#navigation"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Navigation & Power
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#testing"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Testing
                </a>

                <a
                  href="#lessons"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500 transition hover:text-slate-200"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-slate-600 transition-all group-hover:w-16 group-hover:bg-slate-300"
                  ></span>
                  Final Thoughts
                </a>

                <a
                  href="/projects"
                  class="group flex items-center gap-5 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#aaccff] transition hover:text-white"
                >
                  <span
                    class="h-px w-10 bg-[#aaccff] transition-all group-hover:w-16"
                  ></span>
                  Return to Projects
                </a>
              </div>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </header>

        <main class="w-full lg:w-[62%] lg:py-24">
          <section id="overview" class="scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035]"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/robot-hero.png"
                alt="Assembled robot template circuit board"
                class="aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="mt-8">
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                For Science Olympiad, I compete in Robot Tour and Electric
                Vehicle. Both events require a device that traverses a track
                under electrical power, and I had struggled to build a robot
                that could reliably navigate those tracks.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                This robot template is a reusable starting point. It is
                explicitly a work in progress, but the goal is to make the
                electrical platform dependable enough that future builds can
                focus on the event-specific mechanics.
              </p>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="requirements" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Requirements
            </h2>
            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">01</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">Four motors</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  Run up to four motors individually.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">02</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">
                  Independent start
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  Use a button separate from BOOT and RESET so programming does
                  not immediately start the course.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">03</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">Dual power</h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  Support both USB and an external battery supply.
                </p>
              </article>
              <article
                class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-6"
              >
                <div class="text-sm text-[#aaccff]">04</div>
                <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-medium text-white">
                  Direction sensing
                </h3>
                <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-400">
                  Include an onboard sensor for determining direction.
                </p>
              </article>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="electronics" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <div
              class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] md:items-center"
            >
              <div>
                <h2
                  class="mb-8 text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
                >
                  Electronics
                </h2>
                <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  I chose the L293DD motor driver as a surface-mount equivalent
                  of the common L293N. Voltage-regulating capacitors were added
                  to help prevent transients from damaging components.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The microcontroller is an ESP32-S3-WROOM. BOOT and RESET
                  buttons handle programming, while a third button starts the
                  course. A slide switch selects between USB and battery power.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="space-y-4">
                <img
                  src="/images/robot-pcb.png"
                  alt="PCB layout of the robot template"
                  class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
                />
                <img
                  src="/images/robot-schematic.png"
                  alt="Schematic of the robot template"
                  class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="navigation" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Navigation & power
            </h2>
            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
              <div>
                <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  The previous robot used an accelerometer/gyroscope
                  combination, but its drift was too large. This version uses a
                  LIS2MDL magnetometer instead, relying on Earth's magnetic
                  field for an absolute orientation measurement.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="leading-7 text-slate-400">
                  For Electric Vehicle, high speed matters more than finely
                  controlled speed, so the power system uses an LM1084-3v3
                  linear regulator with a maximum current output of 5 A.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div
              class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035]"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/robot-track.png"
                alt="Science Olympiad track layout"
                class="w-full"
              />
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="testing" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Testing & iteration
            </h2>
            <div
              class="mt-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-7 sm:p-9"
            >
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                The first PCB connected to battery power produced the dreaded
                “magic smoke.” Fortunately, the components survived: a copper
                power trace had simply overheated. I bypassed it with a wire
                directly to the slide switch.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                I also discovered that the magnetometer was missing I²C pull-up
                resistors. Those will have to be soldered onto the board before
                the sensor can provide data.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
              <img
                src="/images/robot-battery-test.png"
                alt="Robot board connected to battery and motor"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/robot-motor-test.png"
                alt="Testing a standard DC motor with a large Lego wheel"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
              <img
                src="/images/robot-final.png"
                alt="Robot template circuit board"
                class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/10 object-cover"
              />
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="lessons" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-16 pb-24">
            <h2
              class="text-xl font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-[#aaccff]"
            >
              Final Thoughts
            </h2>
            <div class="mt-8">
              <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
                This project reinforced the idea that simplicity is often the
                path to success. An earlier attempt at an extremely compact
                omnidirectional robot was difficult to solder and debug because
                so many tiny components had to work simultaneously.
              </p>
              <p class="mt-5 leading-7 text-slate-400">
                The robot template has worked exceptionally well for both
                Electric Vehicle and Robot Tour testing, and these boards have
                incredible potential moving forward (even despite the lack of
                sensors).
              </p>
            </div>
            <div
              class="mt-10 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-white/10 pt-6 text-xs text-slate-600"
            >
              <span>Robot Template</span>
              <a href="#overview" class="transition hover:text-slate-300"
                >Back to top ↑</a
              >
            </div>
          </section>
        </main>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
